  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2f4848e7e46289243b311920bdbdddf0, type: 3}
  m_Name: History
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  playerLines:
  - I never really got linear algebra
  - I just see equations and my mind goes blank
  - Huh... I still don't get the equations though
  - <i>huh...</i>
  - <i>So certain equations can only be used when generalising existing equations</i>
  - <i>If I select which equation I want to use, I should be able to also select
    which equations I want to generalise to use my chosen equation</i>
  NPCLines:
  - Linear algebra is a fundamental field of mathematics
  - Sequences of linear equations pop up all over the place and solving them is a
    very important skill
  - What is now known as Gaussian elimination first popped up around the 2nd century
    BCE in <i>The Nine Chapters on the Mathematical Art</i>
  - It has since evolved with the introduction of several concepts such as matrices
    and vector spaces
  - These systems of equations operate on several variables at once
  - These equations are generalisations of certain transformations and such require
    the generalisation of certain numbers to use the equation
  speakTurnPlayer: 010100000000010000010101
